INSERT INTO posts (title, slug, content, excerpt, image_url, categories, tags, author, wp_id, published, created_at, updated_at)
VALUES ('Rural communities in Ireland, Portugal, Finland and Slovenia learning to be more resilient', 'post-254387', 'Those attending heard from outstanding local volunteer Denis Slattery who named the challenges facing villages such as his in Ballylooby, Co Tipperary. While pubs and shops have closed, the village is benefitting from the EU’s Smart Villages initiative.

Denis was a panelist in a discussion on rural resilience which is a key goal of an Erasmus+ action-research project called Rebound.

Dr Brendan O’Keeffe of O’Keeffe Social Research, one of the six Rebound partner organisations, explained the project. The main aim was to devise a solutions-focused course that built capacity while capturing the merits of resilient communities in different types of rural areas in Europe. It involved partners from Lapland in Finland to Slovenia and Portugal. It also promoted the development of digital readiness as a form of resilience. The website ruralresilience.eu/ provides a wealth of information on outcomes and case-studies.

The project led to the launch last September of a Certificate in Rural Resilience which was over- subscribed and which TUS plans to run again this year.

Dr Shane O’Sullivan, TUS, gave a presentation about the course. Students learned skills in evaluation, leadership and advocacy and how to influence policy and advocate for rural communities. The course stresses the importance of equitable resource distribution, respect for cultural diversity, sustainability and community-led local development.

<img src="/files/uploads/2024/07/Gareth-Makim-Dept-of-Rural-and-Community-Development-Ciaran-Lynch-consultant-Dr-Maura-Clancy-TUS-Denis-Slattery-Ballylooby-Dr-Brendan-OKeeffe-social-researcher-and-Dr-Shane-OSullivan-TUS-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="2560" height="1707" /> <em>- Gareth Makim, Dept of Rural and Community Development; Ciaran Lynch, consultant; Dr Maura Clancy, TUS; Denis Slattery, Ballylooby; Dr Brendan O’Keeffe, social researcher; and Dr Shane O’Sullivan, TUS</em>

Gareth Makim from the Department of Rural and Community Development’s Rural Strategy Unit spoke about the Government''s Our Rural Future policy. He said it was “a very good example of modern rural development policy” and noted the Department commissioned the OECD to review the policy. The OECD team visited Ireland in June.

“They will help us identify challenges to come and give us an objective analysis,” he said.

Dr John Morrissey from Mary Immaculate College, Limerick, gave the keynote address - waking some of us from our ignorance about the true societal impacts of climate change. As the author of a new book titled ‘Demanding Sustainability’ he showed why there has to be a societal response to climate change, not just a political one. Only then might humanity see it through intact.

The seminar also heard how farmers are getting a bad rap when it comes to climate change, how the new LEADER programme is “thick with bureaucracy” and off-putting, how volunteers are getting older and why there need to be more paid community development workers.

Mary Mulvey from Co Leitrim was one of 58 students who completed the rural resilience course. She has a background in tourism, heritage and sustainability and describes herself as “always the frustrated person trying to change things”.

“When I saw the advert I said, ‘What’s an hour a week?’ It was exotic connecting from the depths of Leitrim in winter with people in Slovenia, networking together and sharing solutions.

<img src="/files/uploads/2024/07/Mary-Mulvey-in-Thurles-she-described-the-student-experience-doing-the-Certificate-in-Rural-Resilience.jpg" alt="" width="1368" height="1547" /> <em>- Mary Mulvey from Leitrim described the student experience doing the Certificate in Rural Resilience</em>

She said the most striking thing about the course was the need for it.

“The State seems to have gone 360 – every arm of the State wants to interact with communities, but they don’t have the skills or the capacity to do it properly, while communities are consulted to death.

“Where communities are at - at the moment they need an awful lot of help. Some communities are at the end of life stage. We need radical support for communities. Communities can deliver if there’s leadership on the ground and if the State reacts with them,” she said

“And if you’re looking for hope – go to Louisburg in Mayo where they have a community-level climate response project. I met them at the Mary Robinson conference and they have community leaders who know how to manage the State.

“The course was hard. Shorter modules might be better, but in essence the course was fantastic. It was about best practice and people were finding solutions every week. People generally don’t know where to find solutions and people don’t have these spaces to meet. I’m really

happy to have been part of the course. I’ll plug this course every place I can,” she said.

W: ruralresilience.eu/

Twitter: @RuralREBOUND', '“Perpetual challenges” facing rural communities, as well as solutions, were highlighted at a rural resilience seminar held recently on the Thurles campus of the Technological University of the Shannon (TUS).', '/files/uploads/2024/07/Main-Street-Ballylooby.jpg', '[{"slug":"development-work","title":"Development Work"}]', '[{"slug":"certificate-in-rural-resilience","title":"Certificate in Rural Resilience"},{"slug":"community-development","title":"community development"},{"slug":"department-rural-community-development-drcd","title":"Department of Rural and Community Development"},{"slug":"erasmus","title":"Erasmus+"},{"slug":"eu","title":"EU"},{"slug":"leader","title":"LEADER"},{"slug":"mary-immaculate-college","title":"Mary Immaculate College"},{"slug":"okeeffe-social-research","title":"O''Keeffe Social Research"},{"slug":"oecd-organisation-economic-cooperation-development","title":"OECD"},{"slug":"our-rural-future","title":"Our Rural Future"},{"slug":"rebound","title":"Rebound"},{"slug":"rural-development","title":"rural development"},{"slug":"rural-resilience","title":"Rural Resilience"},{"slug":"rural-strategy-unit","title":"Rural Strategy Unit"},{"slug":"smart-villages","title":"Smart Villages"},{"slug":"tipperary","title":"Tipperary"},{"slug":"tus-technological-university-of-the-shannon","title":"TUS Technological University of the Shannon"}]', 'Allen Meagher', 254387, 0, datetime('now'), datetime('now'))
