VALUES ('Toastmaster Eoin Ó Broin - "It''s not easy if you''ve never done it"', 'post-255447', '“I joined in 2017 after I came across them at a summer fair where they had a stall. They meet every fortnight at the Maldron Hotel at Newland’s Cross.

“I found it a bit formal at the start,” he said. Nonetheless, he stuck with it.

Some people join to get confidence ahead of a best man’s speech, or after they have faltered at an important event. As Cllr. Ó Broin recounted:

“I lived in Sweden for a few years and there aren’t that many Irish people there. I got to know the ones who hung out in the Irish pub, or who were involved in the GAA club. One of the lads was getting married, up in the north of Sweden, so we got an overnight train. One of the lads going was really confident. He’d be great craic in the pub, and everyone assumed he’d be the best one to say a few words, and we discussed a few stories.

“At a wedding in Sweden you actually have someone called the Toastmaster and anyone can go up to them and ask them to say a few words. This lad got up to speak on behalf of the groom’s Irish mates. Then he froze, he just said I’d like to raise a glass, but he didn’t tell any of the stories.
<blockquote>“It’s one thing to be confident in a day to day way, but if you’ve never stood up and spoken, it’s not easy if you’ve never done it. Toastmasters is really good for that. But you don’t have to do it the first day or the second day. Everyone helps each other and you learn from people,” he said.</blockquote>
<img src="/files/uploads/2025/09/Gdii2GkXkAAUUpi-e1761707763195.jpeg" alt="" width="1236" height="918" />

Today <a href="https://www.instagram.com/cllreoinobroin/?hl=en">Cllr. Ó Broin</a> is the father of a young family and he faces time constraints and does not attend Toastmasters anymore, but it can be the passion of a lifetime for some people.
“Most people do it for a year or two, but others are lifers, it becomes their main pastime,” he said.', 'A member of South Dublin County Council, Eoin Ó Broin was curious and enthusiastic about Toastmasters once he became aware of it. Like all elected public representatives he needs to be a good communicator.', '/files/uploads/2025/10/Toastmaster-Eoin-O-Broin-with-local-club-stalwarts-Mary-Conlon-and-Pat-Rooney.jpg', '[{"slug":"education-training","title":"Education & Training"}]', '[{"slug":"clondalkin","title":"Clondalkin"},{"slug":"eoin-o-broin","title":"Eoin Ó Broin"},{"slug":"social-democrats","title":"Social Democrats"},{"slug":"toastmasters","title":"Toastmasters"}]', 'Owen Ryan', 255447, 0, datetime('now'), datetime('now'))
