VALUES ('Rathmore Social Action Group recognised in 50th year', 'post-255764', '&nbsp;

<span>It has 35 independent living units for older adults close to local services, while it also runs St Joseph’s Day Care centre. The Centre is open five days a week, offering things like nursing, dementia care, meals on wheels, a laundry service as well as social outlets like bingo and music.</span>

<span>Chief Executive Noreen Fleming said that the award recognises an immense amount of work that has been carried out since it was established in 1975.</span>

<span>“Our founder Jerh O’Donoghue, who was our chairperson until this year, was a teacher in the local secondary school at the time. He was challenging the youth of the area about what they could do and how they could give back to the community. They came up with the idea of helping older people in the locality. It started with going to the bog and collecting turf, helping with laundry, with painting, and visitation. It grew considerably over the decades.”</span>

<span>She said that providing housing for the elderly in the heart of the community is of fantastic value. “When it first started some people were living in very rural areas without access to any public transport. To be here now in the heart of the community, it really changes people’s lives.”</span>

<span>Everyone involved was thrilled with the award, she added.</span>

<span>“It’s fantastic that it is recognised on a national level. It’s fantastic for all of the volunteers and all of the staff from the years gone by. We were delighted to be put forward and absolutely over the moon to receive the award on the night.”</span>

<span>While the recognition has come for what is being done in the area for the elderly, she said there is also a lot on offer to younger members of the community.</span>

<span>“The Social Action Group also has a Youth Group whose members are involved in a diverse range of activities such as fundraising for third world aid and for local charities, organising outings and hosting parties for older adults, participating in the GAISCE Presidents Awards, outdoor and cultural pursuits, discussions and much more. Young people in the group are encouraged to make a genuine effort to brighten up the lives of other people in our community. A Social Club/disco is held for local teenagers on Friday nights, giving them an opportunity to meet friends in a safe environment, to take part in games and finish off with a fun disco. These events are run in Teach Iosagain, our youth and creativity centre which is also used by the community for a number of events and activities.”</span>', 'Fifty years after its foundation, Rathmore Social Action Group from Co Kerry was the winner of the Age Friendly Communities honour at the annual Pride of Place awards.', '/files/uploads/2025/11/he-Social-Action-Group-Rathmore-CLG-Co-Kerry.-1-scaled.jpg', '[{"slug":"community","title":"Community"}]', '[{"slug":"kerry","title":"Kerry"},{"slug":"rathmore","title":"Rathmore"},{"slug":"social-action-group","title":"Social Action Group"}]', 'Owen Ryan', 255764, 0, datetime('now'), datetime('now'))
